# docs/ content conventions

## Language

- Prose: per **AGENTS.md**（e.g. Japanese）
- Filenames & slugs: **English** kebab-case

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `docs/PROJECT_LIFECYCLE.md` | Phases P0–P6, scope H0–H5 |
| `docs/project-state.yaml` | Current phase / gates |
| `docs/requirements/<slug>/` | `要求.md`（P1）, `要件.md`（P2） |
| `docs/design/` | H0–H5 paths（see `docs/design/README.md`） |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture Decision Records |
| `docs/glossary/` | Terms |

Implementation plans: `.agents/plans/` only（PDCA 主: `programs/`, `algorithms/`）.

## User thinking blocks

Use Markdown `>` lines for draft user notes; agents promote confirmed text into body sections.

## Frontmatter（required）

```yaml
---
title: Human-readable title
kind: deliberation | design   # optional on design docs
status: draft | agreed | superseded
created: YYYY-MM-DD
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
---
```

## Body sections（recommended）

- `## Facts` / `## Assumptions` / `## Open questions`

## Links

- Plans: `../../.agents/plans/foo.md`
- Update `docs/README.md` when adding documents

## Do not

- Put implementation plans under `docs/`
- Set `agreed` without explicit user confirmation
